            "review_text": "SMFSanFran\nSan Francisco98 contributions\n0\nGracious and delicious\nSep 2017 • Friends\nMongolian food is, shall we say, interesting. It is a little bit Chinese and a little bit Russian and a little bit mutton and potatoes oriented. But here, at Silk Road, we were served a three course lunch (salad, soup, and main) that was a lovely blend of all of the above. It was such a pleasant luncheon and delicious too. The meat wasn't fatty or tough. The soup wasn't too salty. It was quiet inside, and well decorated, and the wait staff was intent on doing their jobs. It was a lovely lunch!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten September 26, 2017\nHanoi Daewoo Hotel\nDear SMFSanFran,\nThank you for taking time to provide us this valuable feedback. We are glad that you have enjoyed our food and services at Silk Road Restaurant- Hanoi Daewoo Hotel. We look forward to welcoming you back in the near future.\nSincerely,\nThe Hotel Management.\nRead more\nWritten December 13, 2017\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
